ions into the fixed Rust. 22 were caught. I then proved each of the 6 survivors is an *equivalent mutant* (e.g. `add_l(uAB,vAB)`→`add_r` sits behind a `uAB > 0 && vAB > 0` guard, so neither operand can be NaN). One survivor was a genuine gap — `den`×`u` with both NaN — which I closed with three new NaN-provenance tests. `gate2` also asserts the harness loads two *distinct* libraries at different addresses and that its comparators reject a 1-bit diff, `+0.0` vs `-0.0`, and same-value/different-payload NaNs.\n2. **Two C branches are provably unreachable**, documented rather than silently skipped. The `while (iter < 20)` cap can't be hit: proxies have ≤4 vertices, so the `dup` break always fires first — a 1.5M-sample sweep saw a max of 5 iterations. And slot 0's `mul_r(den, u)` is masked by the enclosing `add_r`, whose destination is a later addend.\n\nNo binary/driver exists in either project (`CMakeLists.txt` builds only a `SHARED` lib; the crate is `cdylib`-only), so the stdout-comparison gate item is vacuous — `gjk` is the driver-equivalent entry point and is covered by rows 71–80. `c_src/` was not modified."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":470,"cache_read_input_tokens":245868,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":470,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d13ca368-a34f-4ebf-a098-8de9fa940614","uuid":"6b5e5dd2-3a1e-4a4d-b5f1-57cc402ade01","timestamp":"2026-09-05T08:34:01.930Z"}
